WEBVTT

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.250
What are the chances? [laughs]

00:00:09.458 --> 00:00:11.416
You know, this is
my first time in prison,

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.916
and I gotta say,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.500
their food is on point.

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:18.041
[sighs] How are you even here?

00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:19.333
Destiny.

00:00:19.416 --> 00:00:21.583
Plus an arrest. [chuckles]

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:23.708
But it looks like
Judith got away.

00:00:23.791 --> 00:00:27.875
Was that decision mutual?

00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:29.166
-[sighs]
-Oh.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.833
Sensing trouble in paradise.
Wanna talk about it?

00:00:32.916 --> 00:00:35.166
What I want
is to get out of here.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.583
[Nibbles]
Right, your big plan.

00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:40.000
Lay low on Outback Island
sipping piña koalas.

00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:42.875
Except you can't trust koalas,
'cause they got four thumbs.

00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:45.250
Did a whole episode about it
on my podcast.

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:48.083
It was called
"They Got Four Thumbs."

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:50.208
But you know what? At least
they ain't platypuses.

00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:51.291
-[laughs]
-Wait. Can you just...

00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:53.708
Can you please
just let me concentrate?

00:00:53.791 --> 00:00:54.958
Roger that.

00:00:55.041 --> 00:00:56.000
[crunching]

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:02.250
-Just talk to me, dude!
-[nail cracks]

00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:03.166
[sighs]

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.541
What's the last thing
she said to you?

00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:06.708
[sighs]

00:01:06.791 --> 00:01:08.208
She, um...

00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:14.208
Uh, she said
maybe we are too different.

00:01:14.791 --> 00:01:15.708
[Nibbles] Hmm.

00:01:15.791 --> 00:01:18.458
And what did you say
before that?

00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:21.333
I said the case
isn't worth dying for.

00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:22.458
Mmm.

00:01:22.541 --> 00:01:23.541
Like, uh...

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:29.083
like, you know, as in it isn't
worth her dying for because...

00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:33.458
because solitary animals
like me

00:01:33.541 --> 00:01:36.041
don't have real friends.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:40.625
And I... I...
I don't want to lose her.

00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:43.583
So, I just...

00:01:45.375 --> 00:01:46.750
I don't know how to say that.

00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:49.166
[Nibbles sighs]

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.791
You know what, bud?
I think you just did.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.333
Wait, how'd you do that?

00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:56.166
Well, I opened my arms,

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.000
put them around you
and then I squeezed.

00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:02.333
It's called a hug.
Do foxes not have hugs?

00:02:02.958 --> 00:02:04.333
Oh! [laughs]

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:06.791
The lock.
Yeah, that's Beave 101.

00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:08.916
[Hoggbottom]
The rabbit's in Desert Dunes.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:09.833
Roll out!

00:02:09.916 --> 00:02:11.583
[Truffler] Hit it. Roll out!

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:13.708
Your partner needs you,

00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:16.166
and Nibbles Maplestick
is gonna get you to her.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:22.125
Hey! It's the fox dad!
And the woodchuck!

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.750
Woodchuck? I'm a beaver!
Call me that again--

00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:26.083
-[alarm blaring]
-Oops.

00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:27.958
Okay, go! We gotta go!
Here we go!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.041
Get back here!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.583
[gasps]

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:33.500
Hello, Nicholas.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.583
I hope you like my new home.

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:37.875
I wove it with my own wool.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.041
-Jump scare!
-[Nick screams]

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:45.958
[chuckles]
Adios!

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.083
[cell doors opening]

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:51.291
-[cackling]
-Ooh-whee!

00:02:52.458 --> 00:02:53.708
[inmates shouting]

00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:55.166
[rumbling]

00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:58.583
-[cheering]
-We're free!

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:02.500
-Huh.
-Wheels. We need wheels.

00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:03.416
[horn honks]

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.250
-No, no.
-[tires screeching]

00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:06.750
No, no, no, no.

00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:08.291
I am sorry.

00:03:08.375 --> 00:03:11.208
I do not think we can
get to Judy in time to help.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.916
Unless... [chuckles]

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.333
...you happen to know
the fastest driver

00:03:15.416 --> 00:03:17.375
in the history of Zootropolis.

00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:18.500
[gasps]

00:03:18.583 --> 00:03:22.208
[♪ exciting music playing]

00:03:24.375 --> 00:03:25.375
[♪ music stops]

00:03:33.666 --> 00:03:36.750
[chuckles] Hey, Flash,
Flash Hundred Yard Dash.

00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:37.750
Partner's in trouble.

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:39.291
Need to get across town,
ignore the laws.

00:03:39.791 --> 00:03:40.791
No...

00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:44.791
problem.

00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:46.541
[chuckles] Let's hit it.

00:03:47.375 --> 00:03:48.708
[♪ languid music playing]

00:03:48.791 --> 00:03:50.250
Hey.

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:52.250
-Glad you're here.
-I gotta tell ya,

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:54.791
I'm not convinced
a sloth is our most reliable--

00:03:54.875 --> 00:03:56.291
[both screaming]

00:03:56.375 --> 00:03:58.708
[Nick] Oh, yeah! Whoo-hoo!

00:03:58.791 --> 00:04:00.625
[laughing]

00:04:01.583 --> 00:04:03.041
To turn on the clock tower,

00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:04.375
and light the way
to your great-grandma's home

00:04:04.458 --> 00:04:05.708
so we can find her patent,

00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:08.791
we need to reach the power
control room through here.

00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:10.083
But we have to move quickly
or we're never--

00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:12.583
We shall succeed, Judy Hopps.

00:04:12.666 --> 00:04:14.166
Look, Gary,
if we don't over-prepare,

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.125
we're underprepared
and I don't...

00:04:17.166 --> 00:04:18.833
My family's
been trying to prove

00:04:18.916 --> 00:04:20.458
we're not what everyone thinks

00:04:20.541 --> 00:04:21.875
for a hundred years.

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:25.083
But even this close,
they'd never want me

00:04:25.166 --> 00:04:28.000
to put the weight of the world
on my shoulders.

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:30.458
Because I don't have
any shoulders. [laughs]

00:04:32.041 --> 00:04:34.208
We shall succeed.

00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:40.041
I got you, rabbit.

00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:42.583
[mice scream]

00:04:42.666 --> 00:04:44.791
I cannot help Judy
if I don't know where she is,

00:04:44.875 --> 00:04:46.833
which is why I need you
to get on Paul's computer

00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:48.375
and track Hoggbottom.

00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:50.125
You are an escaped fugitive.

00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:52.541
I could get fired
for even talking to you.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.916
They're gonna put her
to sleep! Do it!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Okay!

00:04:57.541 --> 00:04:58.375
Hmm.

00:04:58.458 --> 00:05:00.875
Did you try restarting it?
Mm-hmm.

00:05:00.958 --> 00:05:02.250
Have you tried
not being an idiot?

00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:04.833
Hey, Paul.
I got you some donuts.

00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:06.291
-Oh!
-[Paul growling]

00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:07.875
-Oh, no!
-Thanks, Clawhauser.

00:05:07.958 --> 00:05:10.208
[Nick]
Clawhauser! Location!

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:15.166
[Pawbert] Oh, no.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.416
I think we're gonna have to
go through the festival.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.625
[Judy] Festival?

00:05:19.375 --> 00:05:20.833
[crowd cheering]

00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:24.333
-[siren wailing]
-[gasps]

00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:26.208
The phone's
the first thing they track.

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:28.041
Go! Go!

00:05:31.416 --> 00:05:33.625
-Clawhauser!
-I am working on it.

00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:37.041
-I got it! No!
-
Great, great, great. Now--

00:05:38.708 --> 00:05:39.958
[Pawbert panting]

00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:46.166
[panting]

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:49.708
Oh. What festival is this?

00:05:53.291 --> 00:05:54.500
Yeah!

00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:55.583
[♪ upbeat music playing]

00:05:57.708 --> 00:05:59.750
Move, move, move!

00:06:01.666 --> 00:06:02.500
[all gasp]

00:06:03.291 --> 00:06:05.375
-Come on!
-Go, go, go!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.041
We are with you, Judy Hopps.

00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:10.416
Ha-ha!

00:06:11.041 --> 00:06:13.083
We meet again, Zebra.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.541
-[knuckles cracking]
-[Zebros yell]

00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:17.375
-Here come the horns!
-Ow!

00:06:20.083 --> 00:06:22.916
She's going for the door.
She's going for the door!

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.958
[Nick]
Clawhauser, we're out of time.

00:06:26.125 --> 00:06:27.125
[Clawhauser] I got it!

00:06:27.791 --> 00:06:29.541
Desert Tundratown weather wall
access door.

00:06:29.625 --> 00:06:32.041
Desert Tundratown weather wall
access door. Hurry!

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:35.500
-What is in that wall?
-Power control room.

00:06:35.583 --> 00:06:38.666
But for, like,
some old part of Tundratown.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.708
[gasps] I know what they're
doing. They'll ruin us.

00:06:44.291 --> 00:06:45.333
[panting]

00:06:45.416 --> 00:06:47.000
[Milton]
No more tranquilizers.

00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:47.958
Put them down.

00:06:48.041 --> 00:06:51.041
-Sir.
-Put them down. Now!

00:06:51.125 --> 00:06:52.666
[♪ tense music playing]

00:06:54.791 --> 00:06:56.333
[Milton]
Take the shot.

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:59.125
Take the shot! Do it!

00:07:00.541 --> 00:07:01.583
Whoa-whoa-whoa!

00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:02.666
[♪ music stops]

00:07:06.541 --> 00:07:08.041
[audio slows, distorts]

